{
  "manufacturer": "Mitsubishi Electric",
  "manufacturer_slug": "mitsubishi-electric",
  "model": "MelcoBEMS MINI (A1M+ / A1M) gateway for Lossnay heat recovery ventilators (LGH and VL series)",
  "model_slug": "melcobems-mini-lossnay",
  "short_model": "A1M+ Lossnay",
  "aliases": [
    "A1M+ Lossnay",
    "MelcoBEMS MINI Lossnay",
    "Procon A1M+",
    "Procon A1M",
    "A1M",
    "Lossnay LGH-RVX Modbus",
    "LGH-15RVX-E1",
    "LGH-200RVX-E1",
    "LGH-150RVXT-E1",
    "LGH-250RVXT-E1",
    "VL-250CZPVU-R-E",
    "VL-500CZPVU-L-E",
    "Lossnay VL Vertical"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handler (heat recovery ventilation unit)",
  "applies_to": "Procon MelcoBEMS MINI A1M+ (manual v1.0.3, firmware 4.1.1) on Lossnay LGH-15..200RVX-E1, LGH-150..250RVXT-E1 and VL-250..500CZPVU-R/L-E; the older A1M (manual v1.1.11) prints the identical Lossnay table.",
  "summary": "Small Procon protocol converter that plugs into a Mitsubishi Electric Lossnay energy-recovery ventilator and serves Modbus RTU on RS-485 or Modbus TCP. For Lossnay units it gives on/off, ventilation mode (heat recovery / bypass / auto) and fan speed control, plus outdoor and room temperature, filter and maintenance signs, fault code, energy use and actual fan speeds.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Every row prints a 0-based 'Addr' next to its Modicon number (40001 = holding 0, 30001 = input 0, 10001 = discrete input 0, 00001 = coil 0). The 0-based Addr is the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "4.1.1",
  "source": {
    "title": "Procon MelcoBEMS MINI (A1M+) Installation Manual",
    "doc_number": "Manual version 1.0.3",
    "revision_date": "2025-09-18",
    "url": "https://library.mitsubishielectric.co.uk/pdf/download_full/5538",
    "pages": "pp. 15-17 (protocols, DIP switches), p. 52 (Modbus TCP), pp. 116-128 (Lossnay Modbus tables), p. 135 (Appendix C compatible Lossnay units)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Only rows the manual ticks for the Lossnay LGH and/or VL series are listed. Every listed row is ticked for both series.",
    "Rows printed with no tick for either series are left out: operating mode (40302), temperature setpoint (40305), supply air temperature (40306 / 30175), CO2 level (40310 / 30179), thermo on/off, actual operation mode, auto fan speed availability, the 0.5 °C step / heat-cool / auto availability flags, the min/max setpoint limits, the temperature-control-unit flags and the supply-air and CO2 sensor flags.",
    "All input registers, discrete inputs and the coil are mirrored as read-only holding registers (power on/off is writable on both holding 300 and coil 3).",
    "Outdoor temperature comes twice: signed (two's complement, down to -56.0 °C) and an unsigned twin for BMSs that cannot handle negative values.",
    "Fan speed value 0 (Auto) is marked not supported on LGH and VL units.",
    "The older MelcoBEMS MINI (A1M) manual v1.1.11, section 13 (https://library.mitsubishielectric.co.uk/pdf/download_full/5186, pp. 37-49), prints the same Lossnay table, addresses and ticks; the A1M is RS-485 only (no Modbus TCP).",
    "DIP switches: 1-5 node address (all OFF = 1, all ON = holding 4), 6 ON = 9600 baud no parity (OFF = holding 5/6), 7 ON = Modbus RTU (OFF = BACnet). Data bits 8 and stop bits 1 are fixed."
  ],
